WEBVTT

00:03.900 --> 00:08.083
If you manage Copilot credits, you're
making the same guess every month.

00:08.083 --> 00:12.323
Give people too little, and they get
cut off in the middle of their work.

00:12.323 --> 00:16.448
Give them too much, and you're paying
for capacity nobody ever touches.

00:17.648 --> 00:21.283
The Cohwork Policy Helper
replaces that guess with evidence.

00:21.283 --> 00:26.129
Load two files, and it tells you the
credit tier every person should actually

00:26.129 --> 00:28.491
on, based on what they really consumed.

00:29.691 --> 00:31.895
Two things fall out of that immediately.

00:31.895 --> 00:34.484
It finds the people about
to hit their ceiling,

00:34.484 --> 00:37.074
so you can protect them
before they're blocked.

00:37.774 --> 00:41.217
And it finds everyone sitting
on an allowance they never use,

00:41.217 --> 00:43.079
so you can bring that money back.

00:44.379 --> 00:46.156
Then it prices the decision.

00:46.156 --> 00:50.344
You see today's committed cost
next to what it becomes if you act,

00:50.344 --> 00:52.057
before anything is applied.

00:53.257 --> 00:57.867
And because it knows about prepaid
credits, it splits that cost into what

00:57.867 --> 01:00.575
already bought and what
is genuinely new spend.

01:00.575 --> 01:02.822
That's the number finance will ask for.

01:04.122 --> 01:07.817
Everything can be cut by department
and measured against a budget,

01:07.817 --> 01:12.519
so each team gets a defensible position
instead of one number for the whole

01:13.719 --> 01:17.025
Then it writes the answer out
for you: a full audit trail,

01:17.025 --> 01:20.389
roll-ups for finance, and a
ready-made deck for leadership.

01:21.689 --> 01:23.159
It's a single web page.

01:23.159 --> 01:27.376
Nothing to install, nothing to
sign into, and nothing is uploaded.

01:27.376 --> 01:31.721
Your data is read in your own browser
and cleared when you close it.

01:33.021 --> 01:37.417
Ten minutes with your own export, and
you'll know what to change and what it

01:37.417 --> 01:40.171
There's a full walkthrough
when you want the detail.
